      },
      "body": "I have a couple questions about the math in the implementation of `neuralop.utils.spectrum_2d`.\n\n1. Why does this function use the L1-norm of the wavenumbers rather than the L2-norm? I believe that using the L2-norm of the wavenumbers is a more standard approach.\n\nhttps://github.com/neuraloperator/neuraloperator/blob/b3abeb1f74a830592f6af3a71060705efde26f35/neuralop/utils.py#L128\n\n2. When performing the binning step, why does the function take the sum of the spectral content within each bin before computing the squared magnitude? I thought the standard approach is to compute the squared magnitudes and then take the sum.\n\nhttps://github.com/neuraloperator/neuraloperator/blob/b3abeb1f74a830592f6af3a71060705efde26f35/neuralop/utils.py#L139\n\nPlease let me know if I am misinterpreting these two lines in the implementation. Thanks!",
