      "body": "I encountered an issue while running the \"Checkpointing and loading training states\" example from the user manual. After using resume_from_dir, the model is not training properly.\r\n\r\nHere is the code I used:\r\n\r\ndevice = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\r\n# device =\"cpu\"\r\ntrain_loader, test_loaders, data_processor = load_darcy_flow_small(\r\n        n_train=1000, batch_size=32,\r\n        test_resolutions=[16, 32], n_tests=[100, 50],\r\n        test_batch_sizes=[32, 32],\r\n)\r\n\r\nmodel = FNO(n_modes=(4,4),\r\n             in_channels=1,\r\n             out_channels=1,\r\n             hidden_channels=4,\r\n             projection_channel_ratio=1,\r\n             factorization='tucker',\r\n             rank=0.42)\r\n\r\nmodel = model.to(device)\r\noptimizer = AdamW(model.parameters(),\r\n                  lr=8e-3,\r\n                  weight_decay=1e-4)\r\nscheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, eta_min=8e-3, T_max=30)\r\nl2loss = LpLoss(d=2, p=2)\r\nh1loss = H1Loss(d=2)\r\n\r\ntrain_loss = h1loss\r\neval_losses = {'h1': h1loss, 'l2': l2loss}\r\n\r\ntrainer = Trainer(model=model, n_epochs=10,\r\n                  device=device,\r\n                  data_processor=data_processor,\r\n                  wandb_log=False,\r\n                  eval_interval=1,\r\n                  use_distributed=False,\r\n                  verbose=True)\r\ntrainer.train(train_loader=train_loader,\r\n              test_loaders={},\r\n              optimizer=optimizer,\r\n              scheduler=scheduler,\r\n              regularizer=False,\r\n              training_loss=train_loss,\r\n              save_every=7,\r\n              save_dir=\"./checkpoints\")\r\n\r\n# .. resume_from_dir:\r\ntrainer = Trainer(model=model, n_epochs=10,\r\n                  device=device,\r\n                  data_processor=data_processor,\r\n                  wandb_log=False,\r\n                  eval_interval=1,\r\n                  use_distributed=False,\r\n                  verbose=True)\r\ntrainer.train(train_loader=train_loader,\r\n              test_loaders={},\r\n              optimizer=optimizer,\r\n              scheduler=scheduler,\r\n              regularizer=False,\r\n              training_loss=train_loss,\r\n              resume_from_dir=\"./checkpoints\")\r\nThe code for saving the model state works fine, but after calling resume_from_dir, the model parameters do not update during training. Based on my testing, it seems that the issue lies in the train_one_epoch function in trainer.py, where the command self.optimizer.step() does not seem to have any effect.",
