      "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nThere seems to be an issue in the tensor contraction when using the separable Fourier convolution option (`separable=True`).\r\nThe problem occurred when I tested the `plot_FNO_darcy.py` example with Tucker contraction as well as in my own toy project. \r\nSeems like the Einstein summation is not correctly set.\r\n\r\nBelow, I only pasted the part of the stacktrace which I deemed most relevant. The full error should be reproducible when adding the above option to the model init in the example.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n`Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"C:\\Users\\Henrik\\virtual_environments\\neuraloperator\\venv\\lib\\site-packages\\tensorly\\plugins.py\", line 72, in cached_einsum\r\n    expression = OPT_EINSUM_PATH_CACHE[key]\r\nKeyError: 'abcd,fghi,bf,eg,ch,di->aecd,(32, 32, 9, 9),(20, 10, 6),(32, 20),(16, 10),(9, 6)'`\r\n...\r\n\r\n` File \"C:\\Users\\Henrik\\virtual_environments\\venv_pytorch\\lib\\site-packages\\opt_einsum\\parser.py\", line 354, in parse_einsum_input\r\n    raise ValueError(\"Number of einsum subscripts must be equal to the \" \"number of operands.\")\r\nValueError: Number of einsum subscripts must be equal to the number of operands.`\r\n",
