      "body": "@zongyi-li \r\n\r\nIt seems that Torch has modified the `fft` to a namespace and put all functions under it: `rfft` and `ifft`, etc.\r\n\r\nBut right now there is no arguments for `one-sided`, and I checked torch's official document, now it seems everything is automatically one-sided unless you want specifically the negative part: [https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/fft.html](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/fft.html). `normalized` arg became `norm`.\r\n\r\nCan you please confirm?",
